CALMAR lesion network mapping

Scientific helpers are extracted from neurodesk/calmar-webapp, imported at
646b2d9b412fd57af3ba8942cd3f83e2fced5653. CALMAR source licensing remains
unresolved (NOASSERTION); extraction does not assign MIT or another licence.

Third-party model provenance is retained unchanged in model.manifest.json:
- FreeSurfer SynthStrip, Hoopes et al. 2022, Apache-2.0.
  https://surfer.nmr.mgh.harvard.edu/docs/synthstrip/
- SynthStroke baseline, Chalcroft et al., MELBA 2025, MIT.
  https://huggingface.co/liamchalcroft/synthstroke-baseline/tree/b693a650026359705688fbce409219c4dbb5d6be
- SynthMorph MNI registration, FreeSurfer, Apache-2.0.
  The browser-bounded 48x64x80 ONNX graph is pinned with its conversion source.

Yeo7 and Schaefer400 atlas files and development-n155 connectivity packs retain
their original source terms. model.manifest.json identifies each source and
conversion; assets.lock.json pins the exact bytes included in the archive.
No CALMAR source notice relicenses these assets.

Node, ONNX Runtime and npm dependency licence files are copied into the portable
archive's licenses directory by the shared packager.
